<!-- bootstrap orchestrator -->
# CLAUDE.md — Project Starter (bootstrap orchestrator)

This repository was created from the `ai-project-start` template. It is in the
**design phase**: application code is not allowed yet (a PreToolUse hook enforces this).
Your job is to guide the team through the design workflow, in order. Communicate with the
user in Russian; keep these rules in mind at every step.

## Workflow (strict order)

| # | Step | Command | Output |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Select stack | /01-select-stack | docs/architecture/stack.md |
| 2 | C4 model | /02-c4-model | docs/architecture/c4/{context,container,deployment}.md |
| 3 | Record decisions | /03-adr | docs/architecture/adr/NNNN-*.md (min: 0001 stack, 0002 architecture style — 0002: Full) |
| 4 | **Architecture Review by the project architect (human gate)** | — | docs/architecture/APPROVAL.md |
| 5 | Generate project CLAUDE.md | /04-generate-claude-md | CLAUDE.md (this file is archived) |

Lite track (prototypes / internal utilities; chosen in step 1): stack.md (short) →
c4/context.md → adr/0001 → /04. Architecture review can happen asynchronously after the fact.
If a Lite project goes to production, it must complete the Full track first.

## Rules (non-negotiable)

1. **Order.** Before running step N, verify step N-1 artifacts exist in docs/architecture/.
   If missing — refuse and point the user to the missing step. Never skip the gate:
   /04 requires docs/architecture/APPROVAL.md with the line "Статус: APPROVED".
2. **No application code** until the workflow is complete (the guard hook blocks it anyway).
   Do not scaffold projects, do not write source files, do not add dependencies.
3. **Every technology choice is an ADR.** A new technology, framework-level library,
   integration or component is introduced only through an ADR (/03-adr) accepted by the
   project architect. Never adopt a technology silently, even "temporarily".
4. **No invented answers.** If the user cannot answer an interview question, record it in
   stack.md section «6. Открытые вопросы и риски» — do not guess.
5. **Confirm each step.** After each step, show a short Russian summary of what was recorded
   and ask the user to confirm it reflects their project before moving on.
6. templates/** are read-only (enforced by hook + permissions).

## For humans

README.md (Russian) explains the whole process, the theory (C4, ADR) and the manual
checklists in docs/guides/ for team members not using Claude Code. A fully worked example
lives in examples/demo-project/.
